# generated by bob
lib/

# React Native Codegen output is not committed. Gradle regenerates it into
# android/build/generated/source/codegen on every build, which is also the only
# way the spec lands in the com.ambirecrypto package that the Kotlin module
# expects — the script that generates shippable codegen hardcodes
# com.facebook.fbreact.specs instead.

# Cargo's build directory. Ignored because it is ~1.6GB of intermediates; the
# artifacts that matter are copied out into jniLibs and ios by ubrn and are
# committed.
rust/target/

# Everything else ubrn produces — the bindings, the platform glue and the
# compiled Rust — is committed on purpose, so a clone can build the app without
# a Rust toolchain. Whoever changes rust/ re-runs `yarn ubrn:android` (and
# `yarn ubrn:ios` on a Mac) and commits the result.
